<http://data.silknow.org/object/e454c316-c6ce-3fb8-a282-e60b7e4ca2bd>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "One side of a pair of woman's boots made of leather lined with woollen felt appliqué and embroidered, from Shache (Yankand), China, ca. 1873"@en , "One side of a pair of boots made of leather lined with red and green woollen felt appliqué, and with elaborately embroidered floral motifs in a combination of silk and woollen threads on its upper and its cuff, and with a blue-painted hemp layered at the top of the pitched cuff. A front vamp lined with magenta-dyed cotton/woollen ends, and edged with chagrin (or shagreen) between its upper and wooden sole and 4 cm high heel painted, and layered with leather at the bottom. Most likely worn by women from the city of Yarkand (also known as Shache in Chinese) at festive occasions."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/1d0fe7a8-5840-320d-b251-7bb207ce52d7> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "One side of a pair of woman's boots made of leather lined with woollen felt appliqué and embroidered, from Shache (Yankand), China, ca. 1873"@en , "One side of a pair of boots made of leather lined with red and green woollen felt appliqué, and with elaborately embroidered floral motifs in a combination of silk and woollen threads on its upper and its cuff, and with a blue-painted hemp layered at the top of the pitched cuff. A front vamp lined with magenta-dyed cotton/woollen ends, and edged with chagrin (or shagreen) between its upper and wooden sole and 4 cm high heel painted, and layered with leather at the bottom. Most likely worn by women from the city of Yarkand (also known as Shache in Chinese) at festive occasions."@en ;
